  \"hr\": {\n./readback/event-184233-as-sent.json:43:          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n./plans/tempo-run.json:6:    {\"label\": \"Warm-up easy\", \"minutes\": 10, \"hr_pct\": [68, 75]},\n./plans/tempo-run.json:8:      {\"label\": \"Tempo\", \"minutes\": 8, \"hr_pct\": [88, 93]},\n./plans/tempo-run.json:9:      {\"label\": \"Float\", \"minutes\": 2, \"hr_pct\": [75, 82]}\n./plans/tempo-run.json:11:    {\"label\": \"Cool-down\", \"minutes\": 5, \"hr_pct\": [65, 72]}\n./readback/watch-notes.md:3:Intervals: LTHR 172. Watch (Forerunner 965): auto-detected LTHR 168, zones\n./readback/watch-notes.md:7:it (see `event-184233-as-sent.json`); `workout_doc.steps` is populated, so the\n./readback/watch-notes.md:17:Every corridor shows up as one of the watch's own zone bands, not the range we\n./readback/watch-notes.md:19:zone edges, never 151–160 or 129–141. Earlier tries: `units: \"bpm\"` with\n./readback/watch-notes.md:21:every target a constant 101.\n./gen.py:2:\"\"\"Build an Intervals.icu event body (workout_doc) from a plan file.\n./gen.py:10:def hr_target(step):\n./gen.py:12:    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n./gen.py:13:    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n./gen.py:18:    if \"hr_pct\" in step:\n./gen.py:19:        out[\"hr\"] = hr_target(step)\n./gen.py:44:        \"workout_doc\": build_doc(plan),\n./README.md:4:exports them to the athlete's Garmin watch through Garmin Connect.\n./README.md:7:  `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` (an event with `workout_doc`).\n./README.md:12:Athlete thresholds live in Intervals (LTHR 172 for this athlete). HR targets\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
